cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the repository as below. When a paper
  describing the platform is published, cite that instead, and see the "How to
  Cite" section of README.md for which publication is the most specific one
  available.
title: GameBrains
abstract: >-
  A research platform where cognitive agents of different architectures play
  repeated n-player games through one interface, with a signed, hash-chained
  experiment ledger and tested adapters to the main multi-agent reinforcement
  learning ecosystems.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Papadopoulos
    given-names: Nikolaos Al.
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1842-8227
    email: nikolaos.papadopoulos@uom.edu.gr
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Applied Informatics, University of Macedonia,
      Thessaloniki, Greece
repository-code: https://github.com/dentros/gamebrains
url: https://github.com/dentros/gamebrains
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - game theory
  - reinforcement learning
  - repeated games
  - cognitive architectures
  - reproducibility
